    "text": "To determine how many cookies each child gets, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Calculate the number of cookies the adults eat.\n2. Determine the number of cookies left after the adults have eaten.\n3. Divide the remaining cookies equally among the four children.\n\nFirst, we calculate the number of cookies the adults eat. Since the adults eat \\( \\frac{1}{3} \\) of the 120 cookies, we have:\n\\[\n\\frac{1}{3} \\times 120 = 40\n\\]\nSo, the adults eat 40 cookies. This means the number of cookies left after the adults have eaten is:\n\\[\n120 - 40 = 80\n\\]\nNext, we divide the remaining 80 cookies equally among the four children. Each child gets:\n\\[\n\\frac{80}{4} = 20\n\\]\nTherefore, each child gets \\(\\boxed{20}\\) cookies.",
